statement:
Let n, k ∈ ℕ, let f : ℝⁿ → ℝᵏ be an arbitrary map (Lean: f : Euclid n → Euclid k, Euclid m = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m)), and let v ∈ ℝⁿ. Write:
- Df(v) := fderiv ℝ f v, by Mathlib's convention the zero map if f is not differentiable at v;
- e_i := EuclideanSpace.single i 1 for i ∈ Fin n;
- fʲ := (w ↦ EuclideanSpace.proj j (f w)) : ℝⁿ → ℝ for j ∈ Fin k, the j-th coordinate of f;
- Dfʲ(v) := fderiv ℝ fʲ v ∈ (ℝⁿ →L[ℝ] ℝ), with its operator norm.
Then Σ_{i∈Fin n} |Df(v)e_i|² ≤ Σ_{j∈Fin k} ‖Dfʲ(v)‖².
